tion.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7aa7ebc3-80d5-541f-813e-64c8db0cc171" :question/math-academy-id "q-97962" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(A-3I)={R}^{3}$\n- **II.** $A-3I$ is singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =3$ is an eigenvalue of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $3$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A-3I) & =3-\\text{nullity}(A-3I) \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{Col}(A-3I)={R}^{3}.$\n\n- Statements II is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ we obtain that $A-3I$ must be non-singular.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=A-3I$ is non-singular, then $(A-3I)x=0$ has only zero solution. As a result, $\\lambda =3$ can not be an eigenvalue of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f28abe1-7ce7-5fcd-800c-5355d28b4dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454274} {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "975b6d1f-67e4-5ad0-a60c-f212c150bba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454275} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e4ad4b-797b-5e1c-957c-e3b4e3622e5b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} {:answer/id #uuid "98e68f38-5fa0-5696-a788-a965baf32116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b268ef17-aa66-5222-b880-47a780072089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454276} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec0d8911-05a3-5867-85d8-d03e8d8a263a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e6411f-f645-554b-849c-9e1f5f16f32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454278} {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df6ff7c-41ab-51b6-a2ff-1f6813596ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8031e5cb-78c7-579e-9e68-cf112703c2a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a33206bb-7969-5524-a745-290fffeff16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97967" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(B-2I)=3,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)=1$\n- **II.** $B-2I$ is non-singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(B-2I) & =4-\\text{rank}(B-2I) \\\\  & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II is false. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(B-2I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $B-2I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=B-2I$ is singular, then $(B-2I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124529 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d1a3a3-a6f0-522c-9161-6dc0fefb2e0d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix and Rank-Nullity Theorems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d33d9c39-fb68-5072-8e1d-d5100f882d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452479} {:answer/id #uuid "31f89fd5-7b10-551c-bc20-cccf8c2d412f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d33d9c39-fb68-5072-8e1d-d5100f882d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452479} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a700a6-056d-5fbf-9c15-802b0bdd40bd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f33abab6-7da2-5b60-9d2f-3f60b47ce8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452481} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9de0a6-d221-54ed-ad32-0d48a983af48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d9de0a6-d221-54ed-ad32-0d48a983af48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452482} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec61757-aa1d-5552-94ae-87ef06754a16" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9364d49b-0c70-5f53-9afc-58a6465fdfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452483} {:answer/id #uuid "bb43d0d6-435a-59ca-b0d6-dd54c6d2f55e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9364d49b-0c70-5f53-9afc-58a6465fdfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452483} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d70d8de-2041-5147-b2df-9b23496268ca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fb578155-2783-5751-8e62-1deb89778f31" :question/math-academy-id "q-97970" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(B-I)=1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(B-I)={R}^{3}$\n- **II.** $B-I$ is singular\n- **III.** $\\lambda =1$ is not an eigenvalue of $B$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $3\\times 3$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=3=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $3$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=3.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(B-I) & =3-\\text{nullity}(B-I) \\\\  & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(B-I)\\ne 3,$ according to invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{Col}(B-I)\\ne {R}^{3}.$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(B-I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $B-I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=B-I$ is singular, then $(B-I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =1$ is an eigenvalue of $B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
